 "proof_level": "host unit tests + compiled SBF with complete provenance + LiteSVM execution of every control row with vault-PDA signatures from a test-only stand-in; no production game instruction is GREEN; no deployment, live Squads, live keys or funds",
 "solana_notes": [
  "A PDA has no private key; it signs only when its owning program calls invoke_signed. Squads vaults are PDAs of the Squads program, so locally a stand-in at that program id is the only way to produce the signature; the main program cannot tell the difference, which is exactly the boundary M14 verifies on devnet with the real Squads program.",
  "ProgramData is the upgradeable loader's record of upgrade_authority: initialize reads it like a canister controller list, except the data lives in the loader's account, not ours; LiteSVM add_program installs a non-upgradeable loader shape, so the fixture rewrites both loader accounts.",
  "Wrapping through the stand-in adds three accounts and about 60 bytes to the packet; the inner instruction's real footprint is what M9 measures."
 ]
